195-- **The prompt carries the standard, not new rules.** Every sentence about what to keep, reject, weigh or open traces to
196-  a line of the step's standard (§8) or a decision; a sentence with no such line is a proposal for Alex, not an edit.
197-  Before writing a reject sentence, check it cannot remove anything the standard keeps: a missing amount, date or scale
198-  is never on its own a reason to drop a statement an analyst would note; its weight is judged apart and may be lower
199-  (D240, Alex: "我不是和你说过不要这么死板吗？这个证据显然是有意义的，不一定什么条件数据时间都要满足，你应该把它记录下来，只是可能档位低一点").
200-  Before any prompt change, audit the whole request (system, every category block, the fixed user sentences, every schema
201-  description and example) against the standard clause by clause, in both directions, with a blind read-only second
202-  reader: each clause is consistent, contradicts, keeps wider, keeps narrower or has no source. Audit the procedure, not
203-  only each sentence's source: a rule that decides by another test than the standard's (2026-10-30: "属于四类、清单没拦住就留"
204-  against the standard's "分析员会不会记") contradicts it even when every sentence quotes the page; so does an exception
205-  written wider than the standard scopes it (2026-10-31: the standard's boundaries each sit on one row, "不能用这一行删掉，
206-  按 5.1 判"; review-v63 gathered them into a closing keep list over every row, and 25 of 32 statements both the gold and a
207-  blind reader reject cited it). Alex, 2026-10-30:
208-  "你需要同时仔细检查prompt和判法准则矛盾的问题，出现很多次了，你应该要做很细的检查".
209-- **A test the model must apply to each statement is a check at the very end of the same prompt.** In one pass the model
210-  keeps what looks like evidence and cites a rule afterwards; rewording the rule, a reason field before each item and a
211-  verdict field after it did not change what it kept (2026-10-30: it marked 95% of its own items "keep"). Asked afterwards
212-  it judged correctly, so the test goes after the item, as a check that reads the list back and returns only what passes,
213-  in the same call. The check is the standard's own test, then its not-kept rows, each carrying its own boundary as the
214-  standard writes it, with the standard's own examples, audited clause by clause like any prompt text; a lost entry is
215-  judged by a blind reader, since a review that merges repeats keeps a different sentence than the gold's (loop log rows 35–49).
216-  Alex, 2026-10-30: "这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于'你刚才说的复核条件'再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面".
217-- **A prompt serves every company, never the bench.** The extraction prompt (and every analyst prompt) is a general
218-  hedge-fund brain: each rule and example must read the same for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip maker.
219-  Examples teach from varied domains; none names the covered company, its products or its numbers, and none is taken
220-  from a test article. A fix is written from the standard and from the request read as the model reads it, not from
221-  the bench's misses, and a prompt is scrubbed for one-company or one-industry wording before any measurement. Alex,
222-  2026-10-29: "It needs to be general purpose as a hedge fund brain. I keep on telling you this, and you keep on
223-  cherry picking the results just to meet the metrics or the benchmarks" (D237).

