docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-v65-round1.md:25:4. **The arrangement row adds a condition that D250 does not have.** Line 3 begins “background **the analyst already knew**: an arrangement the item only describes as in place, with no new step.” D250 says **“只描述一个现成安排……没有新动作的，是背景，不收，文中没写日期也一样”**: an arrangement merely described as already in place, with no new step, is background even without a date. It does not require separately establishing that the analyst already knew the particular arrangement.
