docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-v65-round2.log:69:3. **D250’s analyst-interpretation rule is too wide.** Line 6 rejects “an analyst’s reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation.” D250 and §5.3 say **“具名分析师”**—a *named* analyst—interpreting **“一件已记下的事”**, with no new fact or calculation. [D250](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2975), [standard §5.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:396)
docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-v65-round2.log:75:4. **The arrangement row adds a condition that D250 does not have.** Line 3 begins “background **the analyst already knew**: an arrangement the item only describes as in place, with no new step.” D250 says **“只描述一个现成安排……没有新动作的，是背景，不收，文中没写日期也一样”**: an arrangement merely described as already in place, with no new step, is background even without a date. It does not require separately establishing that the analyst already knew the particular arrangement.
docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-v65-round2.log:81:5. **The product-comparison boundary needs explicit precedence and the required adoption outcome.** Line 5 rejects “a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes” and then says the row “does not cover a competitor’s comparison against the company’s product” or a partner’s or customer’s adoption or integration. D250 says **“只有对手拿来和本公司产品比的按 5.1 判”** and **“同一句里伙伴、客户采用或集成的动作照留”**: judge the competitor’s comparison by §5.1, and keep adoption or integration in the same sentence. [standard §5.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:394)
docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-v65-round2.log:97:- **Line 3:** D250’s “in place,” “no new step” and “even when no date is given” conditions are carried correctly, apart from the added “analyst already knew” condition. The history example is general. Guidance and in-force forecasts and plans need the explicit outcome described above.
docs/research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-v65-round2.log:109:- **Line 9:** The D250 boundary is carried accurately: the check says **“when you cannot say through which path … it moves a question about the company”**; D250 says **“说不出它通过需求、供给、竞争、定价这类路径动了在研公司哪个问题的，不收.”** Both reject mere proximity through an article, event or ecosystem. A path does not automatically keep the matter; it still receives the §5.1 judgment. This is broader than the old v64 row, as D250 requires.
